hello and welcome to hot take the show  where i take a controversial stance and  explain myself as if i was being  interrogated so lately i've been going  through the dragon ball films per your  recommendations some have been pretty  good and others have made me want to  question my choice of career today i've  decided i hate myself enough to watch  the four films recommended the least aka  the worst dragon ball films as chosen or  not chosen by you those are the third  broly movie biobroly curse of the blood  ruby's the very first dragon ball film  sleeping princess and devil's castle the  second dragon ball film and  dragon ball evolution which  if you'd believe it got the same number  of votes as blood rubies and sleeping  princess one vote they each got one  singular vote so let's start with the  most popular of the worst biobroly after  having spent the last few days in norway  on vacation nothing is a greater slap  back to reality than watching biobroly  okay  let's go there the biobroly is easily  one of the strangest films i have ever  seen and that's saying something when  you consider the subject is dragon ball  with weird slapstick and an even weirder  plot biobroly is the only dragon ball  film that doesn't feature goku at all  oh wait it follows goten trunks and  android 18 as they attempt to pick up  the money mr satan owes them for  throwing the tournament but something  interrupts this a very strange man with  an equally strange entrance issues a  challenge to mr satan with motivations  for doing so being equally as childish  and shallow as the original broly film  i'm sensing a trend having been  requested to fight bio warriors mr satan  18 and the two young saiyans make their  way to the headquarters that is  essentially the entire plot to the film  and it brings us up to about eight  minutes worth of run time how long does  the film get oh yeah 46 minutes the  mastermind behind all of this looks  utterly ridiculous and honestly so do  the bio warriors themselves looking more  like putty monsters from the original  power rangers series than actual real  life threats but let's look at some of  the positives huh it is refreshing  getting to see more of android 18 and mr  satan and in places the action is quite  fun most of the comedic moments do fall  flat on their face for me but there are  certain things here and there involving  mr satan that made me giggle okay that's  literally everything i liked in this  movie and pretty much hated everything  else broly's design was probably his  greatest quality in the first film  however in this film they have done away  with any expression and form he once had  in lieu of an animator's nightmare goo  monster it looks utterly ridiculous and  is the main force of antagonism for the  remainder of the film however this  film's greatest sin is the absolute  worst sin any film can have for me it is  so damn boring the film drags its  bioengineered feet from story beat to  story beat but laboring every single  piece of exposition without getting to  the action until we're over half ways  through the feature and the action in  that latter half is so gross to look at  with bio broly lumbering around like a  dung covered sasquatch that it was  honestly a struggle to get through this  entire film this is easily at the bottom  of my list as the worst of these films  i've seen so far and that's pretty much  everything i have to say about biobroly  now on to the one vote club starting  with dragon ball the legend of shenlang  or curse of the blood rubies if you're  looking at the dub and i'm just going to  say it right from the beginning here  this is much better than the votes gave  it credit for but path to power did this  much better as the very first of the now  numerous dragon ball film library this  movie is largely a retreading of the  pilaf saga with pilaf swapped out for a  brand new villain design a brand new  design that is honestly kinda terrible  the movie employs a very classic style  and honestly doesn't age too well in my  opinion there are tons of static scenes  with little to no movement whatsoever  and with its shorter run time of just 50  minutes it spends way too long retracing  the steps of the show and manga in a  much less appealing way might i add all  the while path the power achieved  fantastic success in both of these areas  with that said like paths to power  there's still tons to sink your teeth  into with the variations in the story  and the characters interactions the  classic feel is still very present in  this film if that's something you enjoy  and there's a nice action sequence with  yamcha too that keeps the film from  being too boring during the midpoint  lull with that said the connecting  threads and quote new stuff this film  brings to the table comes in the form of  this little red-headed girl called pansy  who requires the help of goku and the  others to protect her village from the  main villain of the film king gurumez  and he's not interesting at all and if  i'm being completely honest i don't  really care for this film's story  whatsoever mostly because this is a film  that is largely based on the original  material and because path to power had a  much larger pool to draw from curse of  the blood rubies in comparison with the  scene that they chose to introduce are  much less well known and honestly don't  connect all that well at all  additionally a common complaint i've had  with these films has been how they felt  like extended episodes of the show and  thanks to wikipedia i now know why  apparently these films were all designed  such that they represent what the show  currently has to offer visually and  thematically shown across japan at fairs  and festivals to promote the anime and  manga early on these films took the form  of arc recaps like the pilaf saga and  later became spin-offs like cooler's  revenge and fusion reborn stories  inspired and visually similar to the  story being told at that time in the  manga funnily enough these films have  more in common with dragon ball heroes  than they do with battle of gods  resurrection f and the latest broly film  in 2018. and with all that said curse  the blood rubies i didn't really like  this all too much its story is a little  flat convenient and rushed while not  offering much of value at all fingers  crossed our next film does more speaking  of which sleeping princess is tied with  dragon ball evolution with the same  number of votes that being one whether  evolutions was a meme vote or not  doesn't much matter because the only  person voting for sleeping princess was  my editor so this one is about 40  minutes long deep breaths  let's do that  next up is sleeping princess in devil's  castle alrighty so the entire movie is  based around master roshi's training or  at least the early stages where both  krillin and goku attempt to find a girl  to convince roshi to train them the only  difference being that he specifically  asks for someone in particular the  sleeping princess in devil's castle  and that's basically it the story  chronicles how both goku and krillin  tackle his castle and ultimately save  the princess while featuring all of the  regular cast you come to know and love  some of the humor in the race to get to  the castle is fun and the simple plot  really helped this during its short run  time there was one moment in particular  that legitimately made me laugh out loud  when i saw it check it out  straight up i wasn't expecting that  reaction from bulma and it's gotten a  bigger laugh out of me than pretty much  anything the other films has gotten i  should also mention at this time that  bulma as well as the rest of the crew in  their attempt to reach goku managed to  get themselves wrapped up in the castle  situation strangely enough during this  section with goku and krillin exploring  the creepy surroundings it reminded me a  lot of their episode in dragon ball  super where they explored the forest  which as it happens was another fetch  quest issued by roshi amidst the chaos  of the castle launch shows up guns are  blazing and it's honestly really cool to  be perfectly honest i love launch's  design as the blonde version and seeing  her is always a treat turns out she's  just there to collect the diamond which  happens to be the sleeping princess but  all goes downhill from here as launch  sneezes our heroes all get captured by  the villain lucifer yes that's his name  and his evil plan is about to come to  fruition however he didn't bank on one  thing  goku transforming into the uzaru through  the combined efforts of goku and the  rest of the party they all escape  unharmed bringing back launch to meet  master roshi the end honestly this is  exactly the sort of movie i wanted from  early dragon ball there's tons of new  material and it only utilizes plot  points from the manga to set the stage  in a very bare bone sort of way the  villain is fun the adventure is  captivating and the action is so  distinctly old school dragon ball i very  much enjoyed this movie and now finally  dragon ball evolution from 2009. unlike  the vast majority of these dragon ball  films i've rewatched on this channel  evolution was one i actually saw in  theaters day one it was released around  the time i had stopped watching dragon  ball entirely but i was nevertheless  excited to see my favorite characters on  the big screen in order to go see this i  had to convince my family including my  mother and brothers who had no interest  in seeing this film to go with me as i  honestly had no one else to go with so  we made it a family day out so to speak  i still remember the feeling of  embarrassment and confusion i had  leaving the theater that day trying to  convince myself that it wasn't that bad  but let me tell you  it's that bad and a whole lot more  literally nothing in this film works  from the cgi to the choreography to the  casting to the god-awful script this  film was written as though my mother  wrote it we are talking about a script  so fundamentally broken that the writer  of that script issued a public apology  years later stating that he just needed  the money this is a film featuring  characters that are only like the  originals by name and nothing else this  is a film that had help offered by the  license holders including akira toriyama  himself and denied the option this is  the film that inspired akira toriyama to  make battle of gods and start the modern  generation of dragon ball so i guess  something good came out of this mess of  a film a film that even if i was to take  a look at it as its own standalone thing  not taking inspiration from anything is  still a tone-deaf nonsensical amateurish  teen martial arts movie that has no idea  what it actually wants to be what it  wants to say and plays as if it's  embarrassed of what it is this is by far  the single worst most disappointing film  i have ever seen in my life and i refuse  to watch it again and so it's conclusion  time with all the films i've seen over  the last month or so this is what my  rankings of these films looks like right  now at number one as the best dragon  ball film i've seen is path to power  number two is fusion reborn number three  wrath of the dragon number four sleeping  princess in devil's castle was  surprisingly good number five the  world's strongest number six broly the  legendary super saiyan number seven  coolers revenge number eight bojack  unbound number nine curse of the blood  rubies number ten dead zone number  eleven is biobroly and at a distant  number 12 by far the worst dragon ball  evolution now looking at this at first  glance you might be led to believe that  a large chunk of these are actually  pretty good movies but if i'm being  completely honest apart from path to  power and fusion reborn the other films  i've seen have had moments where i had  fun sure but in general didn't offer  enough for me to care to watch them ever  again and when you drop below the fifth  spot on this list there's just awful  film after awful film in my opinion but  that'll do it for this week subscribe  for more if you want to see it and i'll  see you all next week thank you so much  for watching  [Music]

